hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5944","The angels curse the person who points towards his brother with a sharp object, even if he is his real brother."
"5945","I have found elsewhere that the narrator's name is Mu'alla bin Ziyad."
"5946","The Prophet ﷺ prohibited to hand the drawn sword. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2588)"
"5947","The angels curse the person who points towards his brother with a sharp object, even if he is his real brother."
"5948","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No person should point a weapon towards his brother, for he does not know, perhaps Satan may cause it to slip from his hand and the weapon may strike the other person."
"5949","I have narrated to you a hadith from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and yet you are still throwing pebbles. I will never speak to you for such and such a period."
"5950","I do at that time? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do what you consider to be good, and leave what you consider to be evil, and act for your own self, and leave the people to their own state."
"5951","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This will happen when their trusts and their covenants will be mixed with each other, and they will become like this."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) interlaced his fingers. Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Then what is your opinion regarding this?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever you consider good, do it, and whatever you consider evil, do not do it, and act only for your own self, and leave the people (to their own state)."
"5952","We went to Anas bin Malik and complained about the wrong we were suffering at the hand of Al- Hajjaj. Anas bin Malik said, ""Be patient till you meet your Lord, for no time will come upon you but the time following it will be worse than it. I heard that from the Prophet."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 7068)"
"5953","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""If only one night remains before the end of the world, even then a man from the family of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) will surely become a king.\"""""""
"5954","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""If only one night remains before the end of the world, then surely a man from my Ahl al-Bayt will become the ruler in it, whose name will be like my name.\"""""""
"5955","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: A Muslim's best property will soon be sheep which he will take to the tops of the mountains and the places where the rain falls, fleeing with his religion from the civil strife (fitan). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4267)"
"5956","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes, Allah Almighty will admit into Islam whomever He wills from among the Arabs and non-Arabs. The Bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), then what will happen? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then there will come tribulations like darkness. That person said: Never, by Allah! O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! (This will not happen). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes, by Him in Whose hand is my soul (it will happen), and you will again fall into such a situation that you will spread your hoods like snakes and begin to strike off each other's necks. In that time, the best person will be the believer who lives alone in a mountain pass, fears Allah Almighty, and keeps people safe from his own evil."
"5957","“Worship during the time of bloodshed is like emigrating to me.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3985)"
"5958","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: A Muslim's best property will soon be sheep which he will take to the tops of the mountains and the places where the rain falls, fleeing with his religion from the civil strife (fitan). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4267)"
"5959","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon there will come such tribulations which will be like the hot winds; in them, the one who is sitting will be better than the one who is standing, and the one who is standing will be better than the one who is walking. Whoever looks towards them, they will pull him towards themselves."
"5960","I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Try to protect yourself. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: What will you do at that time when people will die, to the extent that a house (meaning a grave) will be obtained in exchange for a servant? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Be patient. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: What will you do at that time when people will fight with each other, to the extent that the place of Hajar Zait will be submerged (in blood)? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Remain where you are (i.e., do not go outside). I said: What is your opinion if they still reach me? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then go inside your house. I said: If they still reach me, what is your opinion? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If you fear that the flash of the sword will disturb you, then place the edge of your sheet over your face; that person will bear the burden of his and your sin. I said: Should I not take up arms against him? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: In that case, you will become equal to him."
"5961","I entered the mosque when 'Abdullah b. 'Amr b. al-'As was sitting in the shade of the Ka'ba and the people had gathered around him. I betook myself to them and sat near him. (Now) Abdullah said: I accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. We halted at a place. Some of us began to set right their tents, others began to compete with one another in shooting, and others began to graze their beasts, when an announcer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced that the people should gather together for prayer, so we gathered around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: It was the duty of every Prophet that has gone before me to guide his followers to what he knew was good for them and warn them against what he knew was bad for them; but this Umma of yours has its days of peace and (security) in the beginning of its career, and in the last phase of its existence it will be afflicted with trials and with things disagreeable to you. (In this phase of the Umma), there will be tremendous trials one after the other, each making the previous one dwindle into insignificance. When they would be afflicted with a trial, the believer would say: This is going to bring about my destruction. When at (the trial) is over, they would be afflicted with another trial, and the believer would say: This surely is going to be my end. Whoever wishes to be delivered from the fire and enter the garden should die with faith in Allah and the Last Day and should treat the people as he wishes to be treated by them. He who swears allegiance to a Caliph should give him the piedge of his hand and the sincerity of his heart (i. e. submit to him both outwardly as well as inwardly). He should obey him to the best of his capacity. It another man comes forward (as a claimant to Caliphate), disputing his authority, they (the Muslims) should behead the latter. The narrator says: I came close to him ('Abdullah b. 'Amr b. al-'As) and said to him: Can you say on oath that you heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He pointed with his hands to his ears and his heart and said: My ears heard it and my mind retained it. I said to him: This cousin of yours, Mu'awiya, orders us to unjustly consume our wealth among ourselves and to kill one another, while Allah says:"" O ye who believe, do not consume your wealth among yourselves unjustly, unless it be trade based on mutual agreement, and do not kill yourselves. Verily, God is Merciful to you"" (iv. 29). The narrator says that (hearing this) Abdullah b. 'Amr b. al-As kept quiet for a while and then said: Obey him in so far as he is obedient to God; and diqobey him in matters involving disobedience to God. (Using translation from Muslim 1844a)"
"5962","“Before the Hour comes, there will be tribulation like pieces of black night, when a man will wake up as a believer but be a disbeliever by evening, or he will be a believer in the evening but will be a disbeliever by morning. And the one who is sitting will be better than the one who is standing, and the one who is standing will be better than the one who is walking, and the one who is walking will be better than the one who is running. So break your bows, cut their strings and strike your swords against rocks, and if anyone enters upon anyone of you, let him be like the better of the two sons of Adam. (i.e. the one killed, not the killer).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3961)"
"5963","The people’s heads were completely still, and they were listening to one person. The narrator says, 'I came and stood near them. Then another person came and stood by my side. I asked this person, ""Who is this gentleman?"" He asked, ""Are you from Basra?"" I replied, ""Yes!"" He said, ""I had guessed so, because if you were from Kufa, you would not ask about this gentleman. This is Sayyiduna Hudhaifah bin Yaman (may Allah be pleased with him), a companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."" I moved closer to him and heard him saying: People used to ask the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about good, and I used to ask the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about evils, because I knew that good would not surpass me. I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Will there be any evil after this good?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""O Hudhaifah, acquire knowledge of the Book of Allah and follow the commands in it."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said this to me three times. I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Will there be any evil after this good?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""There will be trials and evil."" I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Will there be any good after this evil?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""A truce upon impurity (hudnatun 'ala dukhan)."" I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), what is meant by 'a truce upon impurity'?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""People’s hearts will not return to the state they were in before."" I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), will there be any evil after this good?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""O Hudhaifah, acquire knowledge of the Book of Allah and follow the commands in it."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said this three times. He asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), will there be any evil after this good?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""There will be such a trial that will make one blind and deaf. In that tribulation, there will be people who will call towards Hell. O Hudhaifah, if you die in such a state that you are holding onto the trunk of a dry tree with your teeth, that will be better for you than following any one of them."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Yashkari is Sulaiman."
"5964","The people said: Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), but the slave lowered his head. Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) was told: Please step forward (and lead the prayer), so Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: My beloved Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) advised me of three things: that I should obey and follow, even if the ruler is an Abyssinian whose nose and ears are cut off; secondly, that when I make broth, I should add more water to it and then see which of my neighbors I can send it to; and (thirdly) to perform the prayer at its specified time. Then if you come to the Imam and he has already prayed before you, then you have preserved your prayer, otherwise this prayer will be counted as voluntary for you."
"5965","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: There will be a period of commotion in which the one who lies down will be better than the one who sits, and the one who sits is better than the one who stands, and the one who stands is better than the one who walks, and the one who walks is better than the one who runs (to it). He asked: What do you command me to do, Messenger of Allah? He replied: He who has camels should remain with his camels, he who has sheep should remain with his sheep, and he who has land should remain with his land. He asked: If anyone has more of these, (what should he do)? He replied: He should take his sword, strike its edge on a stone, and then escape if he can. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4256)"
"5966","We were one day in the company of 'Umar that he said: Who amongst you has preserved in his mind most perfectly the hadith of Messenger of Allah ﷺ in regard to the turmoil as he told about it? I said: It is I. Thereupon he said: You are bold (enough to make this claim). And he further said: How? I said: I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: There would (first) be turmoil for a person in regard to his family, his property, his own self, his children, his neighbours (and the sins committed in their connection) would be expiated by fasting, prayer, charity, enjoining good and prohibiting evil. Thereupon 'Umar said: I do not mean (that turmoil on a small scale) but that one which would emerge like the mounting waves of the ocean. I said: Commander of the Faithful, you have nothing to do with it, for the door is closed between you and that. He said: Would that door be broken or opened? I said: No, it would be broken. Thereupon he said: Then it would not be closed despite best efforts. We said to Hudhaifa: Did Umar know the door? Thereupon he said: Yes, he knew it (for certain) just as one knows that night precedes the next day. And I narrated to him something in which there was nothing fabricated. Shaqiq (one of the narrators) said: We dared not ask Hudhaifa about that door. So we requested Masruq to ask him. So he asked him and he said: (By that door, he meant) 'Umar. (Using translation from Muslim 144d)"
"5967","I have not left after me any (chance) of turmoil more injurious to men than the harm done to the men because of women. (Using translation from Muslim 2740)"
"5968","The ruin of women is due to two red things: gold and mu'asfar (yellow-dyed cloth or something else)."
"5969","I have not left after me any (chance) of turmoil more injurious to men than the harm done to the men because of women. (Using translation from Muslim 2740)"
"5970","“I am not leaving behind me any tribulation that is more harmful to men than women.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3998)"
"5971","I am the Messenger of Allah?"" He replied: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), but his testimony is of no value."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: ""Does he not perform prayer?"" He replied: ""Yes, he does, but his prayer is of no value."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) then said: ""These are the people whom I have been forbidden (to kill)."
"5972","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us: He belonged to their tribe. He narrates: The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) dispatched an expedition. They attacked a certain people. One man from among them separated himself. One of the members of the expedition went to him with a drawn sword. The (man who had separated) said: \""I am a Muslim,\"" but (the pursuer) did not pay attention to his words and attacked him, killing him. When this news reached the Prophet Muhammad (p"
"5973","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was standing on a camel, and a man was holding the camel’s rein (the narrator is unsure"
"5974","I think these words are also in the narration), and your honor are as sacred to one another as this day is sacred in this city. Soon you will meet your Lord, and He will question you about your deeds. Beware! Do not go astray after me, striking the necks of one another. Let those present convey (this message) to those who are absent, for sometimes the one to whom it is conveyed may preserve it better than the one who heard it directly (from the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him). The narrator states: Whenever the narrator named Muhammad mentioned this hadith, he used to say: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth; it is so. Then the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Beware! Have I conveyed (the message)? Have I conveyed (the message)?"
"5975","I think these words are also in the narration: your honor) are as sacred to one another as this day is in this month in this city. Soon you will meet your Lord, and He will ask you about your deeds. So do not go astray after me, striking the necks of one another. Beware! Let those who are present convey (this message) to those who are absent, for it may be that the one to whom it is conveyed will preserve it better than the one who heard it directly. Beware! Have I conveyed (the message)?"",""Then he said: “Which month is this?” We said"",""“Allah and His Messenger know best.” He remained silent until we thought he would call it by a name other than its own. He said: “Is it not Dhu al-Hijjah?” We said"","" “Yes.”"",""He said: “Which land is this?” We said"",""“Allah and His Messenger know best.” He remained silent until we thought he would call it by a name other than its own. He said: “Is it not the Sacred Land?” We said"","" “Yes.”"",""He said: “Which day is this?” We said"",""“Allah and His Messenger know best.” He remained silent until we thought he would call it by a name other than its own. He said: “Is it not the Day of Sacrifice?” We said"","" “Yes.”"",""He said: “Indeed"",""your blood and your wealth”—Muhammad said: and I think he said"","" “and your honor”—“are sacred to you"","" like the sanctity of this day of yours"","" in this month of yours"","" in this land of yours. And you will meet your Lord"","" and He will ask you about your deeds. So do not return after me astray"","" striking the necks of one another. Let the one who is present convey to the one who is absent"","" for perhaps some to whom it reaches will understand it better than some who heard it. Have I conveyed (the message)?”"""""
"5976","The blood of a Muslim man who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah should not be lawfully shed but only for one of three reasons: married fornicator, soul for soul, and one who deserts his religion separating himself from the community. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4352)"
"5977","""It is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim except in one of three cases: A soul for a soul, a adulterer who has been married, and one who separates leaving his religion."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4721)"
"5978","The narrator states) The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said this due to the severity of the matter, because Allah Almighty has declared the wealth of a Muslim unlawful for another Muslim."
"5979","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""When (a person) an adulterer commits illegal sexual intercourse then he is not a believer at the time he is doing it; and when somebody steals, then he is not a believer at the time he is stealing."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6782)"
"5980","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""For every sin (there is hope) that Allah Almighty will forgive it, except for the person who dies as a polytheist or the one who has intentionally killed a believer."
"5981","""The Messenger [SAW] said: 'If two Muslims meet (and fight) with their swords and one of them kills the other, the killer and the slain will both be in Hell.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4121)"
"5982","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever grants safety to another person regarding his life and then kills him, I am free from the killer, even if the person killed was a disbeliever."" Shaykh Abu Hatim states: Faqitiyan is a branch of the Bajilah tribe, and the people of Qutban (tribe) live in Egypt."
"5983","“No person is killed wrongfully, but a share of responsibility for his blood will be upon, the first son of Adam, because he was the first one to kill.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2616)"
"5984","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Do not kill your children secretly, for the milk, with which a child is suckled while his mother is pregnant, overtakes the horseman and throws him from his horse. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3881)"
"5985","“I shall reach the Cistern (Haud) before you, and I will boast of your great numbers before the nations, so do not fight one another after I am gone.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3944)"
"5986","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Whoever purposely throws himself from a mountain and kills himself, will be in the (Hell) Fire falling down into it and abiding therein perpetually forever; and whoever drinks poison and kills himself with it, he will be carrying his poison in his hand and drinking it in the (Hell) Fire wherein he will abide eternally forever; and whoever kills himself with an iron weapon, will be carrying that weapon in his hand and stabbing his ʿAbdomen with it in the (Hell) Fire wherein he will abide eternally forever."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 5778)"
"5987","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Whoever strangles himself in this world and commits suicide, he will continue to strangle himself in Hell; whoever stabs himself, he will continue to stab himself in Hell; whoever throws himself into the fire and commits suicide, he will continue to throw himself into the fire in Hell."
"5988","I have made Paradise forbidden for him."
"5989","Sayyiduna Jundub bin Abdullah Bajali (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) in this mosque."
"5990","We were along with Messenger of Allah ﷺ in an expedition that a person from amongst the emigrants struck at the back of a person from the Ansir. The Ansiri said: O Ansar! And the Muhijir said: O Emigrants! Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: What are these proclamations of the Days of Ignorance? They said: Messenger of Allah, a person from the emigrants struck at the back of an Ansari, whereupon he said: It is something disgusting. 'Abdullah b. Ubayy heard it and said: They have indeed done it. By Allah, when we would return to Medina the respectable amongst them (the Ansar) would turn away the mean (the emigrants). Thereupon 'Umar said: Permit me so that I should strike the neck of this hypocrite. But he (the Holy Prophet) said: Leave him, the people may not say that Muhammad kills his companions. (Using translation from Muslim 2584b)"
"5991","a Jew killed a young girl for her jewelry, so the Messenger of Allah killed him in retaliation for her. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4740)"
"5992","Has so and so killed you? She indicated with the nod of her head: No. He said for the second time, and she again said: No with the nod of her head. He asked for the third time, and she said: Yes with the nod of her head and Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded to crush his head between two stones. (Using translation from Muslim 1672a)"
"5993","A girl was found with her head crushed between two stones. She was asked: Who has done this to you ? Is it so and so ? Is it so and so, until a Jew was named, and she gave a sign with her head. The Jew was caught ad he admitted. So the Prophet ﷺ gave command that his head should be crushed with stones. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4527)"
"5994","The Prophet ﷺ said: The most merciful of the people in respect of killing are believers (in Allah). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2666)"
"5995","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had long hair, some of which was dyed with henna. He (peace and blessings be upon him) was wearing two green sheets. My father greeted him (peace and blessings be upon him), then he (peace and blessings be upon him) conversed with us for a while. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Is this your son? My father replied: Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, I testify to this. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This son of yours will not bear the punishment for your crime, and you will not bear the punishment for his crime. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse: ""No bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another."" Then my father saw a slightly raised spot between the two shoulders of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! I practice medicine; should I not treat it? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The One who created it will treat it. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The name of Sayyiduna Abu Rimthah (may Allah be pleased with him) is Rifaa’ah bin Yathrabi Taymi. He belonged to Taym Rabaab. Whoever said that the name of Sayyiduna Abu Rimthah (may Allah be pleased with him) is Khushkhash Anbari is mistaken."
"5996","I had relations with a slave woman from Banu so-and-so, and she bore a child. Please give a ruling about my child, that he be given to me. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: He will not be counted as your child, for this is not permissible in Islam. The one against whom a claim is made has more right to take an oath, except in the case where proof is established. The child belongs to the owner of the bed, and for the adulterer, there are stones in his mouth. A man said: O Prophet of Allah (peace be upon him), what is athlab? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Stones. Whoever commits adultery with a woman whom he does not own, or with a woman from another people, and she gives birth to a child, then that child will not be counted as his, nor will he inherit from him, nor will he be made his heir. The believers, in relation to all other people, are like one hand; their lives are equal. If the foremost among them grants protection, the last among them must fulfill it. No believer will be killed in retaliation for a disbeliever, and no dhimmi (non-Muslim under Muslim protection) will be killed during the period of his covenant. People of two religions will not inherit from each other. A woman will not be married together with her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt, and no woman will travel for more than three days without a mahram. And you people will not perform (any voluntary prayer) after Fajr until the sun rises, nor after Asr until the sun sets."
"5997","""I went on a campaign with the Messenger of Allah in the Army of Hardship, and this was the deed of which I was most sure. I had a hired man who fought with another person. One of them bit the finger of the other, who pulled his finger away and a front tooth fell out. He went to the Prophet who considered the tooth to be in vain, and said: ""Would he put his hand in your mouth for you to bite it?"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4769)"
"5998","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Does one of you bite like a camel bites? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) declared (the loss of his teeth) to be without compensation."
"5999","The other man pulled his hand out of his mouth, and his front teeth fell out. So they brought their case to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Does one of you bite his brother’s hand like a camel bites? You will not receive any compensation (diyah)."
"6000","Do you wish to bite as the camel bites? (Using translation from Muslim 1674b)"
"6001","If I were to know that you had been peeping through the door, I would have thrust that into your eyes, and Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Permission is needed as a protection against glance. (Using translation from Muslim 2156a)"
"6002","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""If a person tries to look into your house and you injure his eye, there will be no sin upon you."
"6003","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If a person tries to look into your house without your permission, and you throw a pebble at his eye and blind him, there will be no sin upon you."
"6004","""Whoever looks into a house without the permission of the occupants and they put out his eye, he has no right to blood money or retaliation."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4860)"
"6005","The Messenger of Allah said: ""The injuries caused by the well are without liability, [1] and beasts are without liability, and mines are without liability, and the Khumus is due on Rikaz."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2498)"
"6006","""The injuries caused by the best are without liability, and wells are without liability, and mines are without liability, and the Khumus is due on Rikaz."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2497)"
"6007","“The injuries caused by the beast are without liability, and wells are without liability, and mines are without liability.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2673)"
"6008","The she-camel of Bara' ibn Azib entered the garden of a man and did damage to it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave decision that the owners of properties are responsible for guarding them by day, and the owners of animals are responsible for guarding them by night. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3569)"
"6009","Muhayysah bin Mas'ud and 'Abdullah bin Sahl went to Khaibar for some need they had there, and they parted among the palm trees. 'Abdullah bin Sahl was killed, and 'Abdullah bin Sahl was killed, and his brother 'Abdur-Rahman bin Shl, and Huwayysah, and Musayysah, his paternal cousins, came to the Messenger of Allah. 'Abdur-Rahan spoke about his brother's case, but he was the youngest of them, so the Messenger of Allah said: ""Let the elders speak first."" So they spoke about their companions, and the Messenger of Allah said: Let fifty of your swear an oath."" The said: ""O Messenger of Allah, it is something that we did not witness: how can we swear an oath?"" He said: ""Then let the Jews swear fifty oaths to their innocence."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, they area) a disbelieving people,"" So the Messenger of Allah paid the blood money himself Sahl said: ""I entered a Mirbad of theirs, and one of those camels kicked me."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4713)"
"6010","narrates: In earlier times, people used to kill the murderer in retaliation for the slain, and blood money was not accepted. Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""O you who believe! Retaliation (Qisas) is prescribed for you in the case of those killed,"" up to the end of the verse: ""This is a concession and mercy from your Lord."" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says, so Allah Almighty provided you with a concession in this regard which was obligatory upon those before you, meaning He provided a concession in the form of blood money which was not previously accepted. So whoever accepts blood money, then this will be forgiveness, and there should be a following of goodness, and it should be paid by the one to whom it has been easily forgiven by his brother."
"6011","The one killed in a manner resembling intentional murder but actually killed by mistake—this is the one who is killed with a stick or staff—his blood money will be aggravated, in which there will be forty pregnant she-camels."
"6012","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""The blood-money for the fingers on the hands and (the toes of) the feet is the same: Ten camels for each finger."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1391)"
"6013","I asked: ""Ten, ten (camels)?"" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes."
"6014","The Prophet ﷺ said: The teeth are equal, and the fingers are equal. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4560)"
"6015","“The fingers are the same.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2654)"
"6016","I pay compensation for one who neither cried out nor wailed, who neither drank nor ate anything? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is he using rhymed prose like that of the time of ignorance? Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the payment of compensation obligatory upon the woman’s guardians."
"6017","Two women from the tribe of Hudhail (fought with each other) and one of them threw (a stone at) the other, causing her to have a miscarriage and Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave his verdict that the killer (of the fetus) should give a male or female slave (as a Diya). (Using translation from Bukhārī 6904)"
"6018","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ruled that as compensation for the loss of the child, a slave man or woman should be given. The narrator states: Then the woman who was liable to pay the compensation died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ruled that the payment of her compensation would be obligatory upon her 'asaba (male relatives), while her inheritance would go to her husband and sons."
"6019","About the story of Haml ibn Malik, Ibn Abbas said: She aborted a child who had grown hair and was dead, and the woman also died. He (the Prophet) gave judgment that the blood-wit was to be paid by the woman's relatives on the father's side. Her uncle said: Messenger of Allah! She has aborted a child who had grown hair. The father of the woman who had slain said: He is a liar: I swear by Allah, he did not raise his voice, or drink or eat. No compensation is to be paid for an offence like this. The Prophet ﷺ said: is it a rhymed prose of pre-Islamic Arabia and its soothsaying? Pay a male or female slave of the best quality in compensation for the child. Ibn 'Abbas said: The name of one of them was Mulaikah, and the name of the other was Umm Ghutaif. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4574)"
"6020","Two women from Hudhail fought with each other and one of them hit the other with a stone that killed her and what was in her womb. The relatives of the killer and the relatives of the victim submitted their case to the Prophet ﷺ who judged that the Diya for the fetus was a male or female slave, and the Diya for the killed woman was to be paid by the 'Asaba (near relatives) of the killer. (Using translation from Bukhārī 6910)"
"6021","I had two wives, one of them struck the other and killed both the woman and the child in her womb. Regarding this, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) ruled that as compensation, a slave man or woman should be given, and he also ruled that the woman should be killed in retaliation for the murdered woman."
"6022","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled concerning a fetus that (the blood money) was a slave, male and female. The one against whom this verdict was passed said: ' Should we pay blood money for one who neither ate, drunk, shouted, nor cried, (at the moment of birth)? One such as this should be overlooked .' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'This man speaks like a poet. (But the blood money for a fetus is) a slave, male, or female.'” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2639)"
"6023","The Prophet (peace be upon him) did not leave anything for which he needed to make a bequest. I asked: Then why did he (peace be upon him) command people to make bequests? He replied: He used to instruct them according to the command of Allah Almighty’s Book."
"6024","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: It is the duty of a Muslim man who has something which is to be given as bequest not to have it for two nights without having his will written regarding it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2862)"
"6025","Salim narrates from his father that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a Muslim person that three days pass (and he has not written his will); his will should be with him."
"6026","Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the occasion of the Farewell Hajj, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to visit me because my illness had become severe. I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! You can see the state of my illness. I am a wealthy man and my only heir is my one daughter. Should I give two-thirds of my wealth in charity? The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: No. I said: Half? The Prophet Muhammad (peace be"
"6027","Sayyiduna Shurahbil bin Hasanah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"6028","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Give the wealth to those entitled to fixed shares, and whatever remains after the fixed shares, it will go to the closest male relative."
"6029","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give the prescribed shares to those who are entitled to them, and whatever remains after that will go to the closest male relative."
"6030","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Give the wealth to those entitled to fixed shares, and whatever remains after the fixed shares, it will go to the closest male relative."
"6031","“A grandmother came to Abu Bakr Siddiq and asked him for her inheritance. Abu Bakr said to her: ‘You have nothing according to the Book of Allah, and I don’t know of anything for you according to the Book of Allah, and I don’t know of anything for you according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Go back until I ask the people.’ So he asked the people and Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah said: ‘I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he gave her (the grandmother) one sixth.’ Abu Bakr said: ‘Is there anyone else with you (who will corroborate what you say)?’ Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Ansari stood up and said something like what Mughirah bin Shu’bah had said. So Abu Bakr applied it in her case.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2724)"
"6032","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When a child cries out at birth, his funeral prayer will also be performed and the rulings of inheritance will also apply to him."
"6033","The Prophet ﷺ as saying: A Muslim may not inherit from an infidel nor an infidel from a Muslim. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2909)"
"6034","The daughter will receive half, the granddaughter will receive one-sixth, and whatever remains will go to the sister."
"6035","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""If someone leaves some property, it will be for the inheritors, and if he leaves some weak offspring, it will be for us to support them."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 2398)"
"6036","I am his mawla; I will pay his ransom and inherit his wealth. And whoever has no mawla, his maternal uncle is his mawla; he should pay his ransom and inherit his wealth."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This narration has been heard by Rashid bin Sa'd from Abu 'Amir from Sayyiduna Miqdam (may Allah be pleased with him), and he has also heard this narration from 'Abdur Rahman from Sayyiduna Miqdam (may Allah be pleased with him), and both of its chains are preserved, although the texts of these two narrations differ from each other."
"6037","The narrator states: Those people were practicing this at various places when suddenly a stray arrow came and struck a boy, and that boy died. Among the boy’s relatives, only his maternal uncle was found. Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote a letter to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and described the matter of the boy, asking to whom the blood money should be entrusted. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote back to him that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has said: “Whoever has no mawla (patron), Allah and His Messenger are his mawla, and whoever has no heir, his maternal uncle is his heir.”"
"6038","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) came down from the pulpit for both of them, took hold of them, and said (the command of Allah Almighty is): ""Indeed, your wealth and your children are a trial."
"6039","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a Khutbah to us when Al-Hasan and Al-Husain [peace be upon them] came, wearing red shirts, walking and falling down. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended from the Minbar and carried them, and placed them in front of him. Then he said: 'Allah spoke the Truth: Indeed, your wealth and your children are a trial (64:15). I looked at these two children walking and falling down, and I could not bear patiently anymore until I interrupted my talk and picked them up."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3774)"
"6040","The meaning of) seeing (these) in a dream is steadfastness in religion."
"6041","The truest dreams are those that are seen at the time of Sahar (pre-dawn)."
"6042","“Dreams are of three types: Some are terrifying things from Satan, aimed at causing grief to the son of Adam; some are things that a person is concerned with when he is awake, so he sees them in his dreams; and some are a part of the forty-six parts of prophecy.” He said: “I said to him: ‘Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?’ He said: ‘Yes, I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3907)"
"6043","“A good dream from a righteous man is one of the forty-six parts of prophecy.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3893)"
"6044","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘A righteous dream is one of the seventy parts of prophecy.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3897)"
"6045","The Prophet ﷺ lifted the curtain (and saw that) the people were standing in rows(of prayers) behind Abu Bakr. He said: O people, there remained nothing that gives good tidings from prophethood except a true dream which a Muslim has himself or which another Muslim has for him. I have been prohibited to recite the Qur’an while bowing or prostration. As regards owing, exalt the Lord in it, and as to prostration, make supplication with exertion in it, that is worthy of being accepted. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 876)"
"6046","I conveyed (the message)? He said this three times. (Then he said:) Of the glad tidings of Prophethood, now only dreams remain, which a righteous person sees (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words) or which are shown to him."
"6047","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prophethood has ended and glad tidings (that is, true dreams) remain."
"6048","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the dawn prayer, he would ask: Did any of you have a dream last night? And he said: All that is left of Prophecy after me is a good vision. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5017)"
"6049","narrates: He heard his uncle stating that he heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “A Muslim’s dream is one-fortieth part of prophethood, and it remains in its original state as long as a person does not relate it. When he relates it, then it occurs.”"
"6050","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""The (good) dreams of a faithful believer is a part of the forty-six parts of prophetism:' (Using translation from Bukhārī 6987)"
"6051","He who saw me in dream in fact saw the truth (what is true). (Using translation from Muslim 2267a)"
"6052","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever saw me in a dream has indeed seen the truth (that is, he saw me in the dream), because Satan cannot assume my form."
"6053","narrates from his father that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me in a waking state, because Satan cannot take my form."
"6054","I saw in a dream that I came, then I was taken out of Madinah and admitted into Paradise. I heard a sound, so I investigated, and there were such-and-such and such-and-such persons present. She mentioned the names of twelve men. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had previously sent out an expedition (the woman said). Then those people were brought, they were wearing silk garments and blood was flowing from their veins. Then it was said: Take these people to the river Baydakh. Then they were dipped into it. When they came out, their faces were like the full moon of the fourteenth night. Then a golden tray was brought in which there were dates. They ate from it as much as they wished. Wherever they turned it, they would eat the fruit of their choice from there. I also ate it with them. (The narrator says) Meanwhile, Sayyiduna Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) returned from that expedition and informed: Our situation is such that such-and-such and such-and-such persons have been martyred. Sayyiduna Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioned the names of those twelve men. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) called that woman and said: Relate your dream. The woman began to narrate her dream. She said: Such-and-such and such-and-such persons came, and these were the same names that the man had mentioned (who had been martyred)."
"6055","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""A dream is one-seventieth part of prophethood, and a dream remains suspended until the person who saw it relates it. When he relates it, then it comes to pass. So relate it only before a scholar, or a well-wisher, or a beloved (i.e., a favored person)."
"6056","There came to him (the Holy Prophet) a desert Arab and said: I saw in a dream that I had been beheaded and I had been following it (the severed head). Allah's Apostle ﷺ reprimanded him saying: Do not inform about the vain sporting of devil with you during the night. (Using translation from Muslim 2268c)"
"6057","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever claims to have seen in a dream that which he did not see (i.e., whoever narrates a false dream), he will be made to tie a knot between two grains of barley on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever eavesdrops on people's conversations while they dislike it, molten lead will be poured into his ears on the Day of Resurrection."
